{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DBL83wQAqLYGLjaHQRts3K","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question about KIP controller registration/unregistration metadata record type design decision.\\\\n\\\\n## Design Decision: Create New Metadata Record Type\\\\n\\\\nThe decision was to **create a separate `UnregisterControllerRecord`** rather than reuse existing record types.\\\\n\\\\n**From `/store/discussions/kip-1312-support-unregistering-controllers.md` (lines 117-126):**\\\\n\\\\n> ### Key Design Decisions Confirmed:\\\\n> - **Separate Record**: UnregisterControllerRecord (separate from ApiKey 1)\\\\n>   - Reason: Combined mode (broker + controller) shares node ID\\\\n>   - Without separate record, ambiguous during replay which entity is unregistered\\\\n\\\\n**Rationale:**\\\\n\\\\nThe design team chose a new separate record type because:\\\\n1. In combined mode (where broker and controller run together), node IDs are shared\\\\n2. Without a separate record, it would be **ambiguous during replay** which entity (broker or controller) is being unregistered\\\\n3. A dedicated `UnregisterControllerRecord` eliminates this ambiguity\\\\n\\\\n**Implementation Details:**\\\\n\\\\nFrom `/store/prs/22191-kafka-20395-support-unregistering-controllers.md` (line 26):\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Introduce `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record schema + new MetadataVersion `IBP_4_4_IV2` to support this feature\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis decision was confirmed in Luke Chen's review questions (LC3) during the KIP-1312 discussion, showing the design was well-considered for clarity during metadata log replay.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20247-controller-registration-retry-timeout.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1312-support-unregistering-controllers.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1312-unregistering-controllers.md\\\",\\\"prs/22191-kafka-20395-support-unregistering-controllers.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":24.6,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":66032,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":11940,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0398832,\\\"input_tokens\\\":50,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1870}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22ae4fcd-a410-4492-a375-33fd21cc4f69","uuid":"2508cd82-b99f-470a-9031-cd3f3f5b19ce","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:21:45.114Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question about KIP controller registration/unregistration metadata record type design decision.\\\\n\\\\n## Design Decision: Create New Metadata Record Type\\\\n\\\\nThe decision was to **create a separate `UnregisterControllerRecord`** rather than reuse existing record types.\\\\n\\\\n**From `/store/discussions/kip-1312-support-unregistering-controllers.md` (lines 117-126):**\\\\n\\\\n> ### Key Design Decisions Confirmed:\\\\n> - **Separate Record**: UnregisterControllerRecord (separate from ApiKey 1)\\\\n>   - Reason: Combined mode (broker + controller) shares node ID\\\\n>   - Without separate record, ambiguous during replay which entity is unregistered\\\\n\\\\n**Rationale:**\\\\n\\\\nThe design team chose a new separate record type because:\\\\n1. In combined mode (where broker and controller run together), node IDs are shared\\\\n2. Without a separate record, it would be **ambiguous during replay** which entity (broker or controller) is being unregistered\\\\n3. A dedicated `UnregisterControllerRecord` eliminates this ambiguity\\\\n\\\\n**Implementation Details:**\\\\n\\\\nFrom `/store/prs/22191-kafka-20395-support-unregistering-controllers.md` (line 26):\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Introduce `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record schema + new MetadataVersion `IBP_4_4_IV2` to support this feature\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis decision was confirmed in Luke Chen's review questions (LC3) during the KIP-1312 discussion, showing the design was well-considered for clarity during metadata log replay.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20247-controller-registration-retry-timeout.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1312-support-unregistering-controllers.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1312-unregistering-controllers.md\\\",\\\"prs/22191-kafka-20395-support-unregistering-controllers.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":24.6,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":66032,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":11940,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0398832,\\\"input_tokens\\\":50,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1870}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question about KIP controller registration/unregistration metadata record type design decision.\\n\\n## Design Decision: Create New Metadata Record Type\\n\\nThe decision was to **create a separate `UnregisterControllerRecord`** rather than reuse existing record types.\\n\\n**From `/store/discussions/kip-1312-support-unregistering-controllers.md` (lines 117-126):**\\n\\n> ### Key Design Decisions Confirmed:\\n> - **Separate Record**: UnregisterControllerRecord (separate from ApiKey 1)\\n>   - Reason: Combined mode (broker + controller) shares node ID\\n>   - Without separate record, ambiguous during replay which entity is unregistered\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n\\nThe design team chose a new separate record type because:\\n1. In combined mode (where broker and controller run together), node IDs are shared\\n2. Without a separate record, it would be **ambiguous during replay** which entity (broker or controller) is being unregistered\\n3. A dedicated `UnregisterControllerRecord` eliminates this ambiguity\\n\\n**Implementation Details:**\\n\\nFrom `/store/prs/22191-kafka-20395-support-unregistering-controllers.md` (line 26):\\n> \\\"Introduce `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record schema + new MetadataVersion `IBP_4_4_IV2` to 